cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Privacy Governance Framework, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "Privacy Governance Framework (PGF): Framework Overview and Component Guide"
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Neyman"
    given-names: "Alexey"
  - family-names: "Khvatov"
    given-names: "Val"
abstract: >-
  The Privacy Governance Framework (PGF) is a set of 31 template-and-worked-example documents organised
  in four levels (strategic documents; policies and standards; process model; control, reporting and
  improvement) with a 23-process governance model. It separates statutory legal-compliance gates from
  managerial risk decisions, keeps the Data Protection Officer independent, and uses the GDPR as its
  baseline with adaptation guidance for Canada (PIPEDA and Québec). Documentation release; not legal advice.
keywords:
  - privacy governance
  - data protection
  - GDPR
  - DPIA
  - transfer impact assessment
  - records of processing activities
  - privacy risk
  - privacy by design
  - PIPEDA
  - NIST Privacy Framework

date-released: "2026-10-28"
